<title>BRAZIL: Brazil OKs Deutsche, CS First Boston bank takeovers.</title>
<headline>Brazil OKs Deutsche, CS First Boston bank takeovers.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Monetary Council (CMN) approved Deutsche Bank's takeover of a local brokerage and CS First Boston 's acquisition of the assets of a local investment bank.</p>
<p>A CMN document said the council, Brazil's highest monetary body, authorized Deutsche Bank to take over Sao Paulo-based brokerage Irmaos Guimaraes, which is under Central Bank control.</p>
<p>The CMN also approved CS First Boston's take over of the assets of Banco Investcorp, a Rio de Janeiro-based bank now in the process of being liquidated, the document said.</p>
<p>Under the move, the bank would become 100 percent foreign-owned and would operate as a full-service bank, it added.</p>
<p>((-- William Schomberg, Brasilia newsroom 5561 0258))</p>
